Leave the dirty edits in 'repo/work.c' undisturbed.
In 'repo', add a worktree at '../hotfix' bound to a new branch 'fix'.
Inside 'hotfix', add 'fix.c' containing 'int f;' and commit it with the message 'fix'.
Remove the 'hotfix' worktree and its administrative metadata when done.
Exit the subshell.

Tidbit: 'git worktree add -b <new-branch> <path>' attaches a fresh branch
to a new directory. When finished, 'git worktree remove <path>' cleans
both the directory and its administrative entry in '.git/worktrees'.
